}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/deployments","created_at":"2016-10-05T23:32:51Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T14:51:52Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T14:29:08Z","git_url":"git://github.com/vercel/next.js.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:vercel/next.js.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js","homepage":"https://nextjs.org","size":2429859,"stargazers_count":136480,"watchers_count":136480,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":30029,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3156,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["blog","browser","compiler","components","hybrid","nextjs","node","react","server-rendering","ssg","static","static-site-generator","universal","vercel"],"visibility":"public","forks":30029,"open_issues":3156,"watchers":136480,"default_branch":"canary","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/pulls/60482","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/60482","diff_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/60482.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/60482.patch","merged_at":"2024-01-10T22:14:20Z"},"body":"### What?\r\nWhen using catch-all routes in conjunction with parallel routes, and when importing a client component (`\"use client\"`), the build would fail with the following error:\r\n\r\n> Could not find the module \"PathToClientComponent\" in the React Client Manifest. This is probably a bug in the React Server Components bundler.\r\n\r\n### Why?\r\n`flight-manifest-plugin` generates manifests for each page entry. The `clientModules` portion of this manifest is used by React to load the appropriate client module. When React attempts to render a component tree and detects a module that it cannot find, it will throw this error. To illustrate why it isn't in the tree, consider the following example:\r\n\r\n```\r\napp\r\n  page.tsx\r\n  layout.tsx\r\n  @slot\r\n    [...catchAll]\r\n      page.tsx\r\n```\r\n\r\n```tsx\r\n// app/layout.tsx\r\nexport default function Layout({children, slot}) {\r\n  return <>{children} {slot}</>\r\n}\r\n```\r\n```tsx\r\n// app/@slot/[...catchAll]/page.tsx\r\nimport Link from 'next/link'\r\nexport default function Page() {\r\n  return <Link href=\"/\">Test</Link>\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen visiting `/`, we'd expect both the catch-all `@slot` and the root page to render. At build time, we'll generate a client reference manifest for `/` and `/[...catchAll]` since both are page components. However, the `@slot` imports a client component. When we attempt to load the client reference manifest for `/`, it will ignore the catch-all slot's manifest, resulting in the error.\r\n\r\n### How?\r\nThe `entryNameToGroupName` function seems to already exist to handle this scenario for other cases. For example, `app/(group)/@named/foo/page` needs to know about any manifests associated with `app/foo`. This updates the code to apply similar handling to catchAll segments. When applying this change to the example mentioned earlier, it will properly merge the manifests for both `app/@slot/[...catchAll]/page.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` because both will be part of the `/` group. \r\n\r\nCloses NEXT-1908\r\nFixes #59747\r\nFixes #59510\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/60482/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/60482/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1885816506","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/59747#issuecomment-1885816506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/59747","id":1885816506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBC3Cis5wZ0a6","user":{"login":"sbkobaidze","id":103885846,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjEsFg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103885846?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze","html_url":"https://github.com/sbkobaidze","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbkobaidze/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-10T22:07:59Z","updated_at":"2024-01-10T22:07:59Z","body":"I have the same issue,\r\n\r\n> I have the same issue, the error shows when I import any client component in [...catchAll]/layout.tsx\r\n\r\nExact same situation on my side as well.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos